 "5932": {
  "en": [
   "The ascetic has wakened, there—wakened, there—wakened!",
   "On the laughter-laden south wind he flung away from his body",
   "the heaped pyre-ash of the burning-ground—it has fled, where has it fled?",
   "In the realm of the mind the white light shattered and wakened colour,",
   "A heady passion caught him—caught him in his heart.",
   "Come, all of you, come, all of you, come—",
   "There flows the stream of colour!",
   "A storm of colour surged up in the sky,",
   "Waves of colour on currents of delight rise up wild again and again—",
   "On what spring tide has the flood been called today?",
   "Kettledrums sound, Kanara sounds on the flute—",
   "The stream of weeping has melted into laughter—",
   "It has set a fountain leaping in the heart.",
   "A wind has come rocking us with its word, come to make us lose the path—",
   "A call has come to throw open the doors of the house.",
   "Come, all of you, come, all of you, come—",
   "There flows the stream of colour!",
   "The rising sun, staining it crimson, broke the sleep of the eastern hill",
   "The setting sun steeped itself in that same crimson savour—",
   "and proclaimed the victory-word of everlasting life.",
   "The tune the dawn's vina rang out gathers in the evening sky,",
   "sounding the whole world's music in the silent night's breast.",
   "Come, all of you, come, all of you, come—",
   "There flows the unbound stream of colour!"
  ],
